d8"}], "patch": "patches/9eeedfe8f251dd0258e876b6a1f72efc65a29666-1/20260924T001934Z-29aae09e.patch", "provenance": "verbatim", "runs": {}, "test_sources": [{"commit": "9eeedfe8f251dd0258e876b6a1f72efc65a29666", "paths": ["lexical-parse-integer/src/algorithm.rs"]}], "tests": ["issue_98_test"]}, "shard": "lexical-core", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Patch issue with incorrect parsing of leading zeros.", "summary": "With no_integer_leading_zeros enabled, complete integer parsing incorrectly accepts a zero followed by a non-digit, such as b\"0.1.0\", returning Ok(0). The fix distinguishes a following non-digit from end-of-input and invokes the parser-specific invalid-digit handler: complete parsing returns InvalidDigit(1), while partial parsing returns Ok((0, 1)). Reverse only this match block. The fix adds issue_98_test at the root of lexical-parse-integer/tests/issue_98_tests.rs; it requires features power-of-two and format. No builds or tests were run.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:24:40.393870+00:00"}
